Hi Kamil,
=09
Thank you for reaching out!=20
=09
We're excited to hear about your project and your interest in seeing how St=
able Audio could be a great fit! Please find some feedback on your question=
s below:=20
=09
1. This is dependent on how you choose to use/implement Stable Audio. We cu=
rrently offer 3 options:=20
2. Stable Audio via our Platform API. Our API allows you to access our Stab=
le Audio model suite at a per-audio-generation rate. This option does not r=
equire additional licensing, and you would be free to use your generations =
for any purpose and own full rights to your creations forever.=20
3. Stable Audio via stableaudio.com. This option provides you with a web UI=
 featuring our Stable Audio models. Since your use case would be considered=
 Enterprise, we would work together on an Enterprise agreement, which may a=
llow custom options for pricing and licensing.=20
4. Stable Audio via self-hosting our models. This option allows you to run =
our Stable Audio models on your own infrastructure, which provides the free=
dom to use our model to any capacity. This would also require an Enterprise=
 agreement.=20
5. =09
6. If you decide to use Stable Audio via our Platform API, yes, you may use=
 your outputs as a catalogue, as you have full ownership of your creations.=
 Otherwise, if you decide to use stableaudio.com or self-host the model, an=
 Enterprise Agreement must be in place to use your creations as part of a c=
atalogue.=20
7. The same terms would apply based on how you intend to use Stable Audio.
